ture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-275522" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-337655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product ${I}_{3}B$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${I}_{3}\\cdot B=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-337655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{3}\\cdot B=B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-337655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer