b554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-130243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-130243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & -5 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3\\sqrt{2} & -3.5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$, the result must be the $3$rd column of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3.5 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & -5 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 3\\sqrt{2} & -3.5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 0+3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0+(-3.5)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 0+(-4\\sqrt{5})\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3.5 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f3ee00b57b51bc6bbd65f852437e382da7be7581fe8ff42e6d9d9eaac2faa02"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3.5 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3.5 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-275527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-275527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7\\cdot 0+(-8)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b