050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-275527" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ 0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home