25c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & 1.5 & 2 \\\\ -3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & 1.5 & 2 \\\\ -3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3.5 & -2\\sqrt{3} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f3ee00b57b51bc6bbd65f852437e382da7be7581fe8ff42e6d9d9eaac2faa02"} {"question" "q-41979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/l