gin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f3ee00b57b51bc6bbd65f852437e382da7be7581fe8ff42e6d9d9eaac2faa02"} {"question" "q-41977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -3.2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "q-41977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f050b22ddd2adc712957940b0d2c1107925c54ab9aab554a81c166f6f23daf"} {"question" "e-4408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product $I_3 B$ given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/9b8d8f439845a4949789fe313997d2245249e1a4df58c750d7cda0af36f1ce18.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/example-4408.json" "file_sha256" "d09c2adb71aafbfd9fff7ca18bdb0bf971b0c265e13cc3ee893766b9a12a53a4"} {"question" "e-4408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/ac591cf90fae6e8275fed52c26c8487bff9d654733d414974631948fe30b8150.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/example-4408.json" "file_sha256" "d09c2adb71aafbfd9fff7ca18bdb0bf971b0c265e13cc3ee893766b9a12a53a4"} {"question" "e-4410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product $C D,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/945664c408577aac1d1a745120b3c17c46fd9db93e6d26cc53a4e501390936e2.png)\nand \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/907ffa0b29d96249fe03a7fce3fe682c08982b14c7b7f72840540e6269196425.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/example-4410.json" "file_sha256" "a50e15cdaff929df825faff15273131693e45c878ad039c0891a1a1d816d294e"} {"question" "e-4410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3,$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $C.$ Therefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/980ae75452824b4a8aa701b4e11be8c31448557933357458329f0a2b73a1cca6.png)\n\nDon't believe it? Let's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ -1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/example-4410.json" "file_sha256" "a50e15cdaff929df825faff15273131693e45c878ad039c0891a1a1d816d294e"}] "usage" {"q-130247" [] "e-4410" [] "e-4408" [] "q-75479" []} "basis" 1603 "retractions" [[17592186100609 :question/problem "Calculate the product $I_3 B$ given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186100609 :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186100610 :question/problem "Calculate the product $C D,$ if\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186100610 :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3,$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nDon't believe it? Let's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ -1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186279034 17592186279035 17592186279036 17592186279037 17592186279038 17592186279098 17592186279099 17592186279100 17592186279101 17592186279102] "immutable_fields" [[17592186279033 :answer-field/correct] [17592186279033 :answer-field/id] [17592186279033 :answer-field/key] [17592186279033 :answer-field/type] [17592186279097 :answer-field/correct] [17592186279097 :answer-field/id] [17592186279097 :answer-field/key] [17592186279097 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
